---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="DesignaKnit (DAK) | Knit by Machine"
  description="DesignaKnit is a design-to-knitting system for machine knitters. It helps you work out ideas, then turns those decisions into clear, knit-ready instructions."
>
  <article class="designaknit-page">
    
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section class="hero-section">
      <div class="hero-text">
        <h1>DesignaKnit (DAK)</h1>
        <p class="intro-definition">
          DesignaKnit is a design-to-knitting system for machine knitters. 
          It helps you work out ideas, then turns those decisions into clear, knit-ready instructions — bridging the gap between ideas and knitting.
        </p>
        <p class="intro-support">
          Whether you're planning your first shaped garment or designing something entirely your own, DesignaKnit gives you tools to think through the details before you start knitting.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-image">
        <img 
          src="/images/designaknit/designaknit.webp" 
          alt="DesignaKnit software showing stitch design, garment shaping, pattern layout, and knit-ready instructions"
        />
      </div>
    </section>
    
    <!-- Side-by-side bullet sections with soft panels -->
    <div class="two-column-sections">
      <!-- What Changes Section -->
      <div class="soft-panel">
        <section class="content-section">
          <h2>What changes when you use DesignaKnit</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>You stop guessing and start knowing exactly what to do at each row</li>
            <li>Shaping decisions are worked out ahead of time, not on the fly</li>
            <li>You can resize patterns to fit any gauge or measurement</li>
            <li>Colorwork and stitch patterns become easier to visualize and edit</li>
            <li>Your notes, charts, and instructions live in one place</li>
            <li>Mistakes get caught on screen, not in the knitting</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </div>
      
      <!-- What It Helps You Do Section -->
      <div class="soft-panel">
        <section class="content-section">
          <h2>What DesignaKnit helps you do</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Design garments from scratch using built-in shaping tools</li>
            <li>Create and edit stitch patterns, colorwork, and charts</li>
            <li>Adjust existing patterns to match your gauge and sizing</li>
            <li>Print row-by-row instructions, templates, and charts</li>
            <li>Send patterns directly to compatible electronic knitting machines</li>
            <li>Keep track of your projects and revisit past work easily</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
    
    <!-- Reassurance Section -->
    <section class="content-section reassurance-section">
      <h2>You don't have to use everything at once</h2>
      <p>
        DesignaKnit has a lot of features, and that can feel overwhelming at first. 
        But you don't need to learn it all before you start. Many knitters begin with just one part — 
        like charting a stitch pattern or adjusting a neckline — and explore the rest over time.
      </p>
      <p>
        There's no pressure to master everything. Use what helps you now, and grow into the rest when you're ready.
      </p>
    </section>
    
    <!-- Who It's For Section -->
    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Who DesignaKnit is for</h2>
      <p>
        DesignaKnit is for machine knitters who want more control over their projects. 
        It's especially helpful if you:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Want to design your own garments or modify existing patterns</li>
        <li>Prefer to plan and visualize before you knit</li>
        <li>Use an electronic knitting machine and want to send patterns directly</li>
        <li>Like having clear, printed instructions to follow at your machine</li>
        <li>Enjoy experimenting with stitch patterns, colorwork, or shaping</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="closing-note">
        You don't need to be an expert. DesignaKnit is a thinking tool — it helps you work through decisions at your own pace.
      </p>
    </section>
    
    <!-- Decision-Path Cards Section -->
    <section class="dak-choice-section">
      <h2>Choose your DesignaKnit option</h2>
      <p class="dak-choice-intro">
        All DesignaKnit options use the same core system. The difference is how far you want to take it today. You don't have to choose for your entire future — just where you are now.
      </p>
      
      <div class="dak-choice-grid">
        <!-- Hand Knit Card -->
        <div class="dak-choice-card">
          <h3>Hand Knit</h3>
          <p class="dak-lead">"I'm a hand knitter and I want to write hand-knitting patterns only."</p>
          <ul>
            <li>You design or write hand-knitting patterns</li>
            <li>You want charts and written hand-knitting instructions</li>
            <li>You're not using a knitting machine</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="REPLACE_ME_HAND_KNIT" class="btn-primary">Buy Hand Knit</a>
        </div>
        
        <!-- Standard Card -->
        <div class="dak-choice-card">
          <h3>Standard</h3>
          <p class="dak-lead">"I'm only interested in stitch designs. I won't be creating garment designs."</p>
          <ul>
            <li>You want to create and edit stitch patterns</li>
            <li>You're focused on stitch work, charts, and repeats</li>
            <li>You don't need garment shaping tools</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="REPLACE_ME_STANDARD" class="btn-primary">Buy Standard</a>
        </div>
        
        <!-- Pro Card -->
        <div class="dak-choice-card">
          <div class="dak-card-header">
            <h3>Pro</h3>
            <span class="dak-badge">Sue's Recommendation</span>
          </div>
          <p class="dak-lead">"I will be designing stitch patterns and garments, but I'm not interested in hand knitting instructions or complicated cable instructions."</p>
          <ul>
            <li>You want stitch patterns + garment design</li>
            <li>You care about structure, shaping, and fit</li>
            <li>You don't need hand-knitting outputs or advanced cable complexity</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="REPLACE_ME_PRO" class="btn-primary">Buy Pro</a>
        </div>
        
        <!-- Professional Card -->
        <div class="dak-choice-card">
          <div class="dak-card-header">
            <h3>Professional</h3>
            <span class="dak-badge">Sue's Recommendation</span>
          </div>
          <p class="dak-lead">"I want all of the functionality of DesignaKnit."</p>
          <ul>
            <li>You want the complete DesignaKnit system</li>
            <li>You want maximum flexibility now and later</li>
            <li>You don't want to wonder if something is missing</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="REPLACE_ME_PROFESSIONAL" class="btn-primary">Buy Professional</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <p class="dak-still-not-sure">
        Still not sure? <a href="REPLACE_ME_HELP_LINK">Ask a question</a> before you buy.
      </p>
    </section>
    
    <!-- Final CTA Section -->
    <section class="cta-section">
      <h2>Ready to explore?</h2>
      <p>Find the right option for your knitting, or reach out if you have questions.</p>
      <div class="cta-buttons">
        <a href="/designaknit/compare" class="btn-primary">Choose your DesignaKnit option</a>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn-secondary">Ask a question</a>
      </div>
    </section>
    
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .designaknit-page {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1rem 3rem;
  }

  /* Hero: two-column on desktop, stacked on mobile (text first) */
  .hero-section {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .hero-text {
    order: 1;
  }

  .hero-image {
    order: 2;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .hero-section {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      align-items: center;
    }

    .hero-text {
      order: 2;
    }

    .hero-image {
      order: 1;
    }
  }

  .hero-image img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 8px;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    color: var(--kbm-green);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .intro-definition {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: #333;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .intro-support {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: #555;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Soft Panel styling */
  .soft-panel {
    background: #f0f4ec;
    border: 1px solid #e0e6d8;
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .soft-panel .content-section {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* Two-column bullet sections */
  .two-column-sections {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .two-column-sections {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }
  }

  .content-section {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: #333;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .content-section p {
    color: #444;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .content-section ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .content-section li {
    color: #444;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .reassurance-section {
    background: #f9fafb;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--kbm-green);
  }

  .reassurance-section p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .closing-note {
    font-style: italic;
    color: #666;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* Decision-Path Cards Section */
  .dak-choice-section {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .dak-choice-section > h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .dak-choice-intro {
    color: #555;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    max-width: 700px;
  }

  .dak-choice-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .dak-choice-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .dak-choice-card {
    background: #fafbf9;
    border: 1px solid #e8ebe4;
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .dak-choice-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: #333;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
  }

  .dak-card-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .dak-card-header h3 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .dak-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    background: #e8f0dc;
    color: #4a5d31;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.625rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
  }

  .dak-lead {
    font-style: italic;
    color: #555;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .dak-choice-card ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem 0;
    flex-grow: 1;
  }

  .dak-choice-card li {
    color: #444;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 0.375rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .dak-choice-card .btn-primary {
    align-self: flex-start;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .dak-still-not-sure {
    text-align: center;
    color: #666;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .dak-still-not-sure a {
    color: var(--kbm-green);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .dak-still-not-sure a:hover {
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  /* Final CTA */
  .cta-section {
    background: var(--kbm-bg);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 2rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .cta-section h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .cta-section p {
    color: #555;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .cta-buttons {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.875rem 1.75rem;
    background: var(--kbm-green);
    color: white;
    font-weight: 600;
    border-radius: 8px;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 0.2s;
  }

  .btn-primary:hover {
    background: var(--kbm-green-2);
  }

  .btn-secondary {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.875rem 1.75rem;
    border: 2px solid var(--kbm-green);
    color: var(--kbm-green);
    font-weight: 500;
    border-radius: 8px;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 0.2s;
  }

  .btn-secondary:hover {
    background: rgba(82, 104, 45, 0.08);
  }
</style>
